+RAG execution uses the existing signed step/invocation claims too. The worker puts
+that bearer in `/haive/haive-rag.token`, one run-private read-only extra file beside
+the MCP script, using the same delivery as custom and integration tokens. All MCP
+configuration delivery modes still carry only the shared task bearer in their env;
+the RAG proxy prefers its own token file, so a concurrent agent rewriting a task
+volume cannot select another invocation for attribution. A run without a step
+keeps a task-only token and logs unknown attribution. Legacy env-only proxies remain
+query-compatible and unknown. No new token type, audience or tool argument is used.
